---
import { installationCommand, SKILLS_REPOSITORY_URL, skillsCommand } from '@videojs/installation';

import Aside from '@/components/Aside.astro';
import DocsLink from '@/components/docs/DocsLink.astro';
import A from '@/components/typography/A.astro';
import Code from '@/components/typography/MarkdownCode.astro';
import P from '@/components/typography/P.astro';
import { resolveDocsFramework } from '@/types/docs';

const framework = resolveDocsFramework(Astro.params.framework);
const packageName = framework === 'react' ? '@videojs/react' : '@videojs/html';
const docsIndex = `node_modules/${packageName}/docs/llms.txt`;
const onlineDocsIndex = `/docs/framework/${framework}/llms.txt`;
---

<Aside type="tip" title="Migrate with a coding agent">
  <P>
    If your agent does not have the <A href={SKILLS_REPOSITORY_URL}>Video.js skill</A>, run{' '}
    <Code>{skillsCommand()}</Code> and follow the printed installation and session-reload steps.
  </P>
  <P>
    From your application's root, run <Code>{installationCommand()}</Code> to list installation options. Then request
    a plan with <Code>--framework {framework}</Code>, <Code>--project existing</Code>, and explicit choices for the media,
    source URL, installation method, preset, skin, and extensions. Follow any version-mismatch notice. Both CLI commands
    only print instructions; they do not install packages, edit files, or migrate your player.
  </P>
  <P>
    For an installed package, read <Code class="break-all">{docsIndex}</Code> for documentation matching its version.
    For CDN installations or before installing packages, use the <A href={onlineDocsIndex}>framework docs index</A>{' '}
    and the <DocsLink slug="guides/installation">installation guide</DocsLink>. Keep your existing media URLs and required
    behavior, check this guide's known gaps, and verify playback, captions, controls, and analytics after migration.
  </P>
</Aside>
